# THE SHAPE OF /usr, in one place.  taripnx tars exactly these trees; mkipnx
# lays the tapes down into exactly these and verifies; mkimage extracts and
# verifies the same.  A component list that appears twice will disagree, so
# this file is the only statement of what ipnx.tar carries.
#
# bin and lib are absent deliberately: they are product, not shape -- archive
# objects and binaries a running machine builds and installs onto a disk
# (ipnxbuild, ipnxinstall), never carried in the archive.  ipnx, tmp, adm and
# spool are run-state and stay out for the same reason.
src
man
include
sys
blit
jerq
630
